1
00:00:28,580 --> 00:00:29,980
You

2
00:00:40,200 --> 00:00:43,100
I don't know.

3
00:02:00,000 --> 00:02:00,830
Let's go.

4
00:02:30,000 --> 00:02:31,620
Let's go.

5
00:03:32,500 --> 00:03:33,330
Impossible.

6
00:03:35,960 --> 00:03:37,600
As simple as that.

7
00:03:40,320 --> 00:03:42,280
To happen so easily.

8
00:03:45,320 --> 00:03:49,640
I suppose most of our lives
End pretty much that way.

9
00:03:53,180 --> 00:03:54,817
Not even saying bye.

10
00:03:54,900 --> 00:03:57,020
Just up and drop dead like that.

11
00:03:57,780 --> 00:04:00,074
Damn, lives you feeling kind of lonely?

12
00:04:26,460 --> 00:04:27,637
Don't it.

13
00:04:27,720 --> 00:04:28,960
You bastard.

14
00:04:29,820 --> 00:04:31,520
What did you just say?

15
00:04:31,900 --> 00:04:33,620
Say that again!

16
00:04:36,020 --> 00:04:41,240
Well, looks like little crybaby
Polnareff is trying to talk tough now.

17
00:04:41,900 --> 00:04:42,730
Polnareff!

18
00:04:42,813 --> 00:04:44,289
Don't let him provoke you!

19
00:04:44,640 --> 00:04:45,875
Don't you understand?

20
00:04:46,140 --> 00:04:49,417
Didn't Avdolsan warn you about
the danger of fighting alone?

21
00:04:49,500 --> 00:04:51,340
But you ignored all that,

22
00:04:51,460 --> 00:04:55,320
and now you're trying to take
revenge even if it kills you both!

23
00:04:57,980 --> 00:05:00,540
Then, what am I supposed to do?

24
00:05:01,340 --> 00:05:04,457
Don't fight when there's
absolutely no way you can win.

25
00:05:04,540 --> 00:05:08,157
At the moment, we don't really
understand the nature of their stance.

26
00:05:08,240 --> 00:05:09,740
So just retreat for now.

27
00:05:11,540 --> 00:05:13,900
Avdol was cowardly stabbed from behind.

28
00:05:14,740 --> 00:05:16,840
Are you saying I should run away?

29
00:05:17,120 --> 00:05:19,897
Don't fight a battle that
may cost you your life.

30
00:05:19,980 --> 00:05:22,627
That's what Avdol-san
was trying to tell you.

31
00:05:28,160 --> 00:05:32,100
Hmm, just what the hell's all
that jabbering about you two?

32
00:05:32,340 --> 00:05:34,340
I'm ready whenever you are, right?

33
00:05:34,840 --> 00:05:37,060
Well, ready to lose?

34
00:05:40,220 --> 00:05:41,050
Polnareff!

35
00:05:41,133 --> 00:05:43,300
Don't let up, Zondai!

36
00:05:43,860 --> 00:05:44,690
Get in vain!

37
00:05:58,120 --> 00:05:59,840
Damn it.

38
00:06:01,200 --> 00:06:02,460
All right.

39
00:06:09,960 --> 00:06:12,440
I'm sorry, Polnareff.

40
00:06:17,600 --> 00:06:19,720
Polnareff! Huh?

41
00:06:26,200 --> 00:06:28,460
That guy, Avdol, died for you.

42
00:06:28,720 --> 00:06:30,560
I guess you owe him one, right?

43
00:06:30,920 --> 00:06:34,096
If you hadn't been here, he
wouldn't have died, right?

44
00:06:37,440 --> 00:06:39,980
Damn, where's that bastard's main body?

45
00:06:40,340 --> 00:06:42,120
Poledeth, just stay calm!

46
00:06:44,140 --> 00:06:45,320
But you know what?

47
00:06:45,540 --> 00:06:47,837
There's no need to be sad, Palmerev.

48
00:06:47,920 --> 00:06:50,240
You'll see Avdol soon.

49
00:06:50,800 --> 00:06:54,080
And your precious little sister as well.

50
00:06:55,160 --> 00:06:55,990
What?

51
00:06:56,900 --> 00:07:02,000
When you meet your little sister again,
why don't you ask her how I killed her?

52
00:07:16,340 --> 00:07:17,880
Don't take the bait!

53
00:07:18,140 --> 00:07:20,280
He's just trying to provoke you!

54
00:07:22,520 --> 00:07:23,350
Bastard!

55
00:07:36,240 --> 00:07:41,160
It's impossible for your
chariot to cut my hanged man.

56
00:07:42,760 --> 00:07:49,340
I exist inside the mirror, where
your stand is unable to reach me.

57
00:07:50,040 --> 00:07:51,360
Are you frustrated?

58
00:07:51,760 --> 00:07:52,740
I'm sure.

59
00:07:55,340 --> 00:07:57,660
Hey, whole horse, shoot him.

60
00:07:57,940 --> 00:07:59,997
Let's finish off this idiot.

61
00:08:00,080 --> 00:08:03,320
Yes, sirreeee!

62
00:08:12,820 --> 00:08:14,220
Die!

63
00:08:43,480 --> 00:08:47,357
Polnareff was shot by...

64
00:08:47,440 --> 00:08:48,640
Emerald Splash!

65
00:08:51,680 --> 00:08:53,740
To save Polnareff's life!

66
00:09:03,220 --> 00:09:05,749
Damn, they're out of
the range of my stand.

67
00:09:06,240 --> 00:09:10,280
Even if it hits the target, it's
too far away for maximum impact.

68
00:09:14,720 --> 00:09:16,180
I guess Mr. J.

69
00:09:16,380 --> 00:09:19,717
Giles hell-bent on ridding the
world of that Polnareff fella.

70
00:09:19,800 --> 00:09:20,630
Hmm?

71
00:09:23,620 --> 00:09:25,620
My apologies, Kakyoin.

72
00:09:26,440 --> 00:09:29,877
If I could have avenged my sister's death,

73
00:09:29,960 --> 00:09:32,657
I wouldn't have minded
being killed in the attempt.

74
00:09:32,740 --> 00:09:36,440
But now I think I understand
what Avdol tried to tell me.

75
00:09:37,240 --> 00:09:39,700
His sacrifice will not go to waste.

76
00:09:40,140 --> 00:09:42,120
I will fight and survive.

77
00:09:46,680 --> 00:09:50,860
So, Polnareff, do you
truly understand now? Yeah.

78
00:09:59,000 --> 00:10:02,420
That's in lieu of
shaking hands to make up.

79
00:10:06,220 --> 00:10:08,957
Now they're no longer just your enemy.

80
00:10:09,040 --> 00:10:11,620
The next time they attack us?

81
00:10:13,200 --> 00:10:15,880
You and I will bring them down!

82
00:10:35,320 --> 00:10:36,360
That was close.

83
00:10:36,620 --> 00:10:38,796
I'm at a fair disadvantage by myself.

84
00:10:39,480 --> 00:10:42,360
I've never been one to
be the lone gunslinger.

85
00:10:42,620 --> 00:10:45,091
Hell, there'll be another chance later on.

86
00:10:46,280 --> 00:10:48,460
I'm sure I stabbed him with my sword.

87
00:10:51,460 --> 00:10:53,200
But apparently I missed him.

88
00:10:53,700 --> 00:10:55,280
I felt no resistance.

89
00:10:58,360 --> 00:11:03,200
His stand, the Hanged Man, can launch
an attack from any reflective surface.

90
00:11:03,660 --> 00:11:05,517
Even the smallest fragment will do.

91
00:11:05,600 --> 00:11:09,160
The Hanged Man attacks my
reflection from inside the mirror.

92
00:11:09,620 --> 00:11:13,520
But there's no way I can get myself
into something like a mirror.

93
00:11:13,920 --> 00:11:17,760
How the hell am I supposed to
fight someone like him? Shit!

94
00:11:22,120 --> 00:11:22,950
Palmadeth

95
00:11:23,520 --> 00:11:25,297
You keep saying things like.

96
00:11:25,380 --> 00:11:26,617
Inside the mirror.

97
00:11:26,700 --> 00:11:28,717
Or the world of the mirror.

98
00:11:28,800 --> 00:11:31,257
But there's no such world inside there.

99
00:11:31,340 --> 00:11:32,797
What the hell are you saying.

100
00:11:32,880 --> 00:11:34,377
You saw it too, didn't you.

101
00:11:34,460 --> 00:11:35,977
He exists in the mirror.

102
00:11:36,060 --> 00:11:37,877
But when you turn around, he's not there.

103
00:11:37,960 --> 00:11:41,197
Yes, but a mirror is just
a reflection of light.

104
00:11:41,280 --> 00:11:43,177
Nothing more to it than that.

105
00:11:43,260 --> 00:11:45,037
Listen, I don't need you to tell me that.

106
00:11:45,120 --> 00:11:46,357
Of course I know that.

107
00:11:46,440 --> 00:11:49,460
I'm not talking about
common knowledge here!

108
00:11:52,080 --> 00:11:54,380
If something like a stand can exist,

109
00:11:54,900 --> 00:11:59,312
I'm telling you it's not so strange
that a world inside a mirror can exist!

110
00:12:03,180 --> 00:12:04,100
Now what?

111
00:12:04,320 --> 00:12:07,357
I suppose you still have some
sort of a problem with that?

112
00:12:07,440 --> 00:12:12,540
No, but I do think the mystery of his
true nature is somehow related to that.

113
00:12:13,680 --> 00:12:18,280
And somehow, his true nature
is also his greatest weakness.

114
00:12:34,380 --> 00:12:35,210
Polareff!

115
00:12:35,293 --> 00:12:36,857
He's in the chrome on the steering wheel!

116
00:12:36,940 --> 00:12:37,770
What?

117
00:12:58,420 --> 00:13:00,100
Kakyoin, you okay?

118
00:13:00,980 --> 00:13:06,260
My chest really hurts, but I'll manage.

119
00:13:21,040 --> 00:13:23,480
Get away from anything reflective.

120
00:13:27,000 --> 00:13:27,840
That's it.

121
00:13:28,040 --> 00:13:28,920
Now I get it.

122
00:13:30,100 --> 00:13:30,930
Mirrors.

123
00:13:31,013 --> 00:13:34,937
He followed us here from mirror to
mirror by a series of reflections.

124
00:13:35,020 --> 00:13:38,360
Reflections, which means
it's actually light.

125
00:13:38,800 --> 00:13:41,560
Its true nature is a stand of light.

126
00:13:42,540 --> 00:13:46,237
Don't go near any reflective objects and
remove anything like that from your body,

127
00:13:46,320 --> 00:13:47,150
too.

128
00:13:50,460 --> 00:13:53,377
My brothers, it looks like
you had a car accident.

129
00:13:53,460 --> 00:13:54,813
You must need medicine.

130
00:13:55,740 --> 00:13:56,700
Buy from me.

131
00:13:56,840 --> 00:13:58,369
I can give you a discount.

132
00:14:02,240 --> 00:14:03,070
What?

133
00:14:03,153 --> 00:14:04,440
Come on, buy it.

134
00:14:04,600 --> 00:14:05,718
I'll make it cheap.

135
00:14:07,600 --> 00:14:08,600
The bastard.

136
00:14:09,000 --> 00:14:10,160
In a child's eye.

137
00:14:11,320 --> 00:14:12,150
Hey, kid!

138
00:14:12,540 --> 00:14:14,305
Don't look at us, you hear me?

139
00:14:15,760 --> 00:14:16,737
Everything's fine.

140
00:14:16,820 --> 00:14:19,232
See, there's nothing wrong with us, okay?

141
00:14:19,580 --> 00:14:21,933
Now get away from here, you little brat!

142
00:14:26,020 --> 00:14:27,480
You damn bastard!

143
00:14:29,140 --> 00:14:30,440
Wait! Pull that F!

144
00:14:33,000 --> 00:14:34,360
What will you do now?

145
00:14:34,700 --> 00:14:38,935
You wouldn't poke this little boy's
eyes out with your sword, would you?

146
00:14:44,720 --> 00:14:46,360
I've got you at last.

147
00:14:46,540 --> 00:14:50,760
You can't escape now unless
you poke out this boy's eyes.

148
00:14:56,180 --> 00:14:59,180
Poke out this boy's eyes, you say? Shit.

149
00:15:00,140 --> 00:15:05,380
Stabbing Avdol-san from behind and
now using a child unforgivable.

150
00:15:07,600 --> 00:15:08,760
Hey, Kakyoin.

151
00:15:08,940 --> 00:15:12,240
In this situation, you don't
use a stock line like that.

152
00:15:12,540 --> 00:15:17,340
Listen, when the time comes to take
revenge, this is the kind of line you use.

153
00:15:18,840 --> 00:15:21,540
My name is Jean-Pierre Polnareff.

154
00:15:21,720 --> 00:15:25,017
For all your crimes, for the
honor of my sister's spirit,

155
00:15:25,100 --> 00:15:27,920
and so that my friend
Abdel may rest in peace.

156
00:15:31,980 --> 00:15:35,568
Without fail, I will drive you
to the very depths of despair.

157
00:15:40,220 --> 00:15:41,340
Forgive me, kid.

158
00:15:55,740 --> 00:15:57,500
There, in Polnareff's eyes.

159
00:16:03,000 --> 00:16:06,840
I'm not sure how it works, but he
can move at the speed of light.

160
00:16:07,320 --> 00:16:09,437
Normally, it's a speed
beyond all recognition.

161
00:16:09,520 --> 00:16:14,167
But if that kid's eyes were to close, I
knew his next move would be to my eyes.

162
00:16:14,700 --> 00:16:17,357
And if you can predict that path...

163
00:16:17,440 --> 00:16:20,720
Then cutting him with my sword is easy!

164
00:16:26,520 --> 00:16:27,350
Over there!

165
00:16:27,620 --> 00:16:28,860
Let's go, Kakyoin!

166
00:16:32,100 --> 00:16:33,380
Ah! The medicine!

167
00:16:39,520 --> 00:16:52,140
Let's go!

168
00:16:52,800 --> 00:16:54,857
Let's go! Let's

169
00:16:54,940 --> 00:17:01,460
go!

170
00:17:03,520 --> 00:17:04,920
Bastard! Finally!

171
00:17:14,960 --> 00:17:16,540
At last we meet, eh?

172
00:17:17,200 --> 00:17:18,580
Mr. J. Guile.

173
00:17:34,640 --> 00:17:37,320
Yes, I figured out your Stan's secret.

174
00:17:38,420 --> 00:17:41,060
Frankly, your stand surprised me at first.

175
00:17:41,420 --> 00:17:45,217
Although it was clearly visible, there
was nothing I could do to counter it.

176
00:17:45,300 --> 00:17:49,100
But once I understood its true
nature, it was no big deal.

177
00:17:49,400 --> 00:17:51,760
You can kiss your ass goodbye now!

178
00:17:53,440 --> 00:17:56,320
So, allow me to finish you off slowly.

179
00:18:03,700 --> 00:18:08,320
This is not Jake Isle!

180
00:18:14,320 --> 00:18:15,420
Pull it off!

181
00:18:19,320 --> 00:18:20,150
Shit!

182
00:18:31,860 --> 00:18:37,680
Gee, Kyle, you're just a stupid
fool after all, eh, Boulder F?

183
00:18:38,240 --> 00:18:41,000
You don't even know what I look like,

184
00:18:41,160 --> 00:18:44,260
yet you carelessly approached,
thinking you'd won!

185
00:18:44,760 --> 00:18:46,917
That guy's just a street peddler.

186
00:18:47,000 --> 00:18:52,060
All I had to do was cut him with a knife
in the same place you injured the hangman.

187
00:18:53,940 --> 00:18:54,770
Bastard!

188
00:18:54,853 --> 00:18:55,800
Hold on now.

189
00:18:56,020 --> 00:18:57,560
Take a good look around.

190
00:18:58,680 --> 00:19:00,180
Hey, got around.

191
00:19:01,280 --> 00:19:04,660
These travelers would like to
give all of you some money.

192
00:19:10,520 --> 00:19:11,780
What's going on?

193
00:19:32,720 --> 00:19:35,760
Do you realize what this means?

194
00:19:48,020 --> 00:19:48,850
Ha ha!

195
00:19:48,933 --> 00:19:51,000
You say you've figured out my stand?

196
00:19:51,300 --> 00:19:52,140
You fool!

197
00:19:52,380 --> 00:19:55,556
It's my stand, so naturally
I'm aware of its weakness.

198
00:19:56,120 --> 00:20:00,077
Increasing the number of reflective
objects will make his path unpredictable,

199
00:20:00,160 --> 00:20:01,937
and no longer will it be vulnerable.

200
00:20:02,020 --> 00:20:02,850
Don't look!

201
00:20:02,933 --> 00:20:03,763
Everyone, stop looking at us!

202
00:20:06,120 --> 00:20:07,860
Now you can't escape,

203
00:20:08,180 --> 00:20:13,380
or are you going to create an exit by
slaughtering the poor innocent peddlers, huh?

204
00:20:16,220 --> 00:20:19,480
Polnareff, you sacrificed
your youth to pursue me.

205
00:20:19,900 --> 00:20:22,380
Oh, how sad that you failed.

206
00:20:23,720 --> 00:20:26,980
Oh, what a lonely,
wretched life you've led.

207
00:20:27,460 --> 00:20:29,700
But don't worry, Polnareff.

208
00:20:29,880 --> 00:20:33,500
After you leave this world,
I will live happily on in it.

209
00:20:33,620 --> 00:20:36,640
Women at my feet,
catering to my every need.

210
00:20:38,340 --> 00:20:40,280
Is it us they want to see?

211
00:20:40,960 --> 00:20:41,837
Or that?

212
00:20:41,920 --> 00:20:45,720
By the way, what an
entertaining little screamer!

213
00:20:52,100 --> 00:20:53,920
Your sister was...

214
00:20:58,620 --> 00:21:00,320
Bastard! Just wait!

215
00:21:00,560 --> 00:21:02,325
I'm coming up there right now!

216
00:21:05,820 --> 00:21:08,897
Polneneff, such words
are not appropriate here.

217
00:21:08,980 --> 00:21:12,017
When the time comes to
take revenge you shouldn't

218
00:21:12,100 --> 00:21:14,880
use words like bastard
you say it like this

219
00:21:16,020 --> 00:21:21,397
My name is Noriyaki Kakyoin
so that my friend Abdo Sol and

220
00:21:21,480 --> 00:21:25,640
the soul of my friend Alnaref's
sister will rest in peace

221
00:21:27,080 --> 00:21:31,080
may Jay Gile atone for
these crimes with his life

222
00:21:34,080 --> 00:21:37,340
I will give that gold coin
to whoever picks it up.

223
00:21:42,480 --> 00:21:46,300
It's a gold coin, so shiny
you can see your face in it!

224
00:21:46,940 --> 00:21:48,120
I got it!

225
00:21:48,340 --> 00:21:49,800
I understand, Kakyoin!

226
00:21:54,220 --> 00:21:55,200
Right there!

227
00:22:03,200 --> 00:22:04,030
Chariot!

228
00:22:17,840 --> 00:22:19,577
A-a

229
00:22:19,660 --> 00:22:26,020
-a-a-a-a!

230
00:22:51,600 --> 00:22:56,160
You are the one who's so
good at screaming, J. Guile.

231
00:22:56,320 --> 00:22:57,420
I was wrong.

232
00:22:57,680 --> 00:23:00,700
I'll do whatever you say,
so please forgive me.

233
00:23:01,420 --> 00:23:06,760
My sister, my younger sister must
have said the same thing to you.

234
00:23:07,520 --> 00:23:09,320
But you killed her anyway.

235
00:23:09,760 --> 00:23:12,600
You killed her for your own sick pleasure.

236
00:23:14,060 --> 00:23:17,440
How long have I waited for this moment?

237
00:23:19,540 --> 00:23:22,640
From here, you'll be
screaming your way to hell.

238
00:23:22,840 --> 00:23:26,369
But there are things I can't
leave to the demons down there.

239
00:23:27,380 --> 00:23:28,210
Die!

240
00:23:59,280 --> 00:24:01,120
Oh, my God.

241
00:24:31,920 --> 00:24:36,060
A very fitting end for
someone named the Hanged Man.

242
00:24:43,140 --> 00:24:44,964
This ain't no damn good for me.

243
00:24:46,240 --> 00:24:48,475
I'm at a hell of a disadvantage alone.

244
00:24:48,820 --> 00:24:52,761
Without a partner to back me up,
my gunfighting skills can't shine.

245
00:24:52,920 --> 00:24:55,280
Better to be number two than number one.

246
00:24:55,500 --> 00:24:57,340
That's my philosophy in life.

247
00:24:57,740 --> 00:24:59,505
I best get on out of here now.

248
00:25:05,000 --> 00:25:05,830
Bastard.

249
00:25:17,660 --> 00:25:19,480
Jotaro! Joseph-san!

250
00:25:20,180 --> 00:25:22,940
We already know all about Avdol.

251
00:25:23,300 --> 00:25:27,020
Time was short, so we gave him
a simple but proper burial.

252
00:25:29,120 --> 00:25:31,700
So, what should we do with this guy?

253
00:25:33,440 --> 00:25:37,160
The bastard who stabbed Avdol-san
in the back was J. Guile.

254
00:25:37,700 --> 00:25:41,288
But this guy is the one who
fired the bullet that killed him.

255
00:25:42,700 --> 00:25:43,640
I see.

256
00:25:49,940 --> 00:25:51,240
That settles it.

257
00:25:52,960 --> 00:25:55,320
Let me be the one to carry out justice.

258
00:25:56,300 --> 00:25:57,359
Spare me, partner.

259
00:25:57,560 --> 00:25:59,384
I'll do anything you ask, okay?

260
00:25:59,540 --> 00:26:02,011
Every one of them begging for their lives.

261
00:26:02,660 --> 00:26:05,317
I'll teach you that you
can't get off so easy.

262
00:26:05,400 --> 00:26:07,660
So, prepare to learn!

263
00:26:09,820 --> 00:26:13,040
Please run, my dearest
hole horse. It's you.

264
00:26:13,620 --> 00:26:15,738
Please, please run while I hold him.

265
00:26:16,020 --> 00:26:18,000
You're my only reason for living.

266
00:26:18,420 --> 00:26:19,997
Please escape while you can.

267
00:26:20,080 --> 00:26:21,480
Who is this woman?

268
00:26:24,660 --> 00:26:26,780
Thank you so much for saying that.

269
00:26:26,980 --> 00:26:31,760
I gladly accept your offer and will
live on to see another sunrise. Bastard!

270
00:26:32,220 --> 00:26:33,397
Dearest hole horse!

271
00:26:33,480 --> 00:26:36,657
You know, I'm only running
away because I love you, honey.

272
00:26:36,740 --> 00:26:40,757
Otherwise, we won't be able to go on
like this, loving each other forever.

273
00:26:40,840 --> 00:26:42,660
See you, baby. Love you.

274
00:26:44,920 --> 00:26:45,750
Wait!

275
00:26:58,080 --> 00:26:58,910
Shit!

276
00:27:01,860 --> 00:27:04,177
This woman! Stop it! Polnareff!

277
00:27:04,260 --> 00:27:07,672
But that bastard killed Avdol
and she helped him get away!

278
00:27:07,880 --> 00:27:10,617
We just can't afford to
go chasing after him now.

279
00:27:10,700 --> 00:27:14,700
It's unfortunate, but we don't have
the time to make any side trips.

280
00:27:16,060 --> 00:27:16,890
That's right.

281
00:27:17,340 --> 00:27:19,517
In keeping with Avdol-san's intentions,

282
00:27:19,600 --> 00:27:23,776
we need to put this matter aside for
now and continue with our journey.

283
00:27:25,380 --> 00:27:26,400
All right!

284
00:27:37,580 --> 00:27:38,410
Avdol.

285
00:27:40,180 --> 00:27:42,260
May your soul rest in peace.

286
00:27:42,600 --> 00:27:44,659
We will join you there soon enough.

287
00:27:47,580 --> 00:27:48,698
Let's go, everyone.

288
00:27:48,960 --> 00:27:51,078
Let's continue our journey to Egypt.

289
00:27:53,480 --> 00:27:55,720
Look, Dio isn't going to be easy.

290
00:27:56,020 --> 00:27:59,617
If the four of us want to beat this enemy,
we're going to have to stick together.

291
00:27:59,700 --> 00:28:03,397
If any one of us gets out of line,
he's sure to take advantage of it.

292
00:28:03,480 --> 00:28:04,320
Be careful.

293
00:28:07,860 --> 00:28:10,360
How can he say something like that to us?

294
00:28:10,540 --> 00:28:13,617
In his own way, he's dealing
with the trouble he's caused,

295
00:28:13,700 --> 00:28:15,940
including the incident with Avdol.

296
00:28:19,580 --> 00:28:21,160
Oh, what a pain.

297
00:28:29,920 --> 00:28:33,320
Come on! Move it! Huh? Oh!

298
00:28:38,740 --> 00:28:41,200
Avdol, you wait and see.

299
00:28:41,800 --> 00:28:44,540
I promise I will avenge your death.

300
00:29:06,800 --> 00:29:10,380
No, my son just died.

301
00:29:22,820 --> 00:29:28,720
My dearest son, you perished.

302
00:29:29,040 --> 00:29:32,420
Your body covered with horrible
wounds just like these.

303
00:29:34,340 --> 00:29:36,520
Oh, you're agony.

304
00:29:37,420 --> 00:29:40,820
I can feel it through the
pain of the astigmata.

305
00:29:41,900 --> 00:29:45,000
God damn it, I'll fucking kill you.

306
00:29:45,580 --> 00:29:49,860
I'll damn well make sure I
killed you with my own hands.

307
00:29:50,660 --> 00:29:52,880
With my own stand.

308
00:29:53,540 --> 00:29:54,370
Justice!

309
00:30:03,480 --> 00:30:04,560
Oh, my God.
